      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are a couple of issues with it related to type safety. For example `AP_POWER_PRE_INIT | AP_POWER_STARTUP` is not of type `enum ap_power_events`. So the naive approach would be to cast the `events` argument. But we\u0027re expecting the user to `|` the arguments already so technically the inbound argument is likely not `enum ap_power_events` anyway. Overall, if we\u0027re going to use it as a bit mask, it makes sense to use a uint32_t or uint16_t.",
      "parentUuid": "d7ecf99c_12a9a925",
